multi_index_map 0.15.1 — MIT License
  Repository : https://github.com/lun3x/multi_index_map
  crates.io  : https://crates.io/crates/multi_index_map
  Copyright  : Copyright (c) 2022 Louis Wyborn
  License text: third_party/LICENSES/multi_index_map-MIT.txt
  Note       : Upstream master was read at 2026-10-14 (its Cargo.toml already
               declares 0.16.0); the published 0.15.1 is the pinned reference.
  Concepts referenced (no code copied):
    - record store + one lookup table per indexed field, four index quadrants
      (hashed/ordered x unique/non-unique)
    - non-unique index as key -> ordered set of slot ids
    - slot table with holes that keeps ids stable across removals
    - "uniqueness violation leaves the container completely unchanged"
    - per-index iterators, and iterating an index by retrieving from the store
  Deliberate deviations from this reference are documented in
  docs/SPEC.md (section 0.3) and CHANGELOG.md (Notes / Deviations).

