SUPPORTING REFERENCES (concepts only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
slotmap 1.1.1 — Zlib License
  https://github.com/orlp/slotmap
  Concept: slot + generation stable keys, free-list reuse, sparse secondary maps.

thunderdome 0.6.1 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/LPGhatguy/thunderdome
  Concept: generation bumped on slot reuse; explicit, tested overflow behaviour.

indexmap 2.14.2 — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  https://github.com/indexmap-rs/indexmap
  Concept: making the cost of removal explicit (swap_remove vs shift_remove).
  Also the origin of the Robin Hood engine adapted in the author's
  aurasuisui/indexmap (Apache-2.0).

bimap 0.6.3 — Apache-2.0 OR MIT (dual-licensed; upstream writes "Apache-2.0/MIT")
  https://github.com/billyrieger/bimap-rs
  Concept: reporting an overwrite structurally (Overwritten enum) instead of
  discarding it. The author's aurasuisui/bimap is a MoonBit port of this crate.

hecs 0.11.2 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/Ralith/hecs
  Concept: separating the stable handle table from the movable physical storage.

bevy_ecs 0.20.0 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy
  Concept: ComponentSparseSet (dense + sparse arrays) for dense integer keys.

Boost.MultiIndex (C++), BSL-1.0
  https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_79_0/libs/multi_index/doc/index.html
  Concept origin of the multi-index container model (via the reference above).

